9e5fa993 Change GK collisionless Maxima to experiment with a scheme that uses a discontinuous phi, and thus a DG Hamiltonian (dgH). The approach here is to compute a weak form of the Yushmanov gradient using the gk_collisionless_flux kernels. This weak stencil uses an upwinding/LF-flux form in the surface term, where the penalty term has the opposite sign as the streaming term flux. Then we use that Yushmanov gradient in computing characteristics, instead of taking gradients of the Hamiltonian. The hope is this will remove instabilities in sub-sonic regimes. I don't think it's working yet though.
